# Prices, as each place feels them (Docs/Design/30-towns-and-talk.md): Ridgemere's Houses, wharf, salt pans and Sump,
# the haul up the High Road to Frosthollow, and the towns' own trades. Blanks: {item}, {price}.
# Alternatives run in parallel.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Ridgemere

scene em_rm_pr_sump
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=ridgemere
a : In the Sump they're boiling fish heads for supper. | #topic.what# at #topic.price#. The Sump will starve before the Houses notice. | The Sump children are begging at the Commons Market again.
b : Fish heads are better than nothing. | The Houses notice. They just don't care. | Every day this week.
a : Barely. | Exactly. | And every day they're thinner.
b?[noble] : The Houses give alms every Restday.

scene em_rm_pr_vesk_fish
when topic=prices topic.dir=up topic.item=meal here.region=ridgemere
a : The Fish Hall sets the price of fish and fish sets the price of supper. | Smoked fish at the wharf costs more than fresh used to. | The smokehouses are full and the stalls are bare. Explain that.
b : The Fish Hall sets the price of everything wet. | Smoke costs money. | Easy. They're waiting for the price to climb.
a : And everything here is wet. | So does salt. | That's exactly it.
b?[fisher] : We catch it. The Fish Hall sells it. We see none of the difference.

scene em_rm_pr_rain_hall
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=ridgemere
a : The Council of Houses could fix prices in an afternoon. | Somebody should take #topic.price# for #topic.what# to the Rain Hall. | The Rain Hall leaks and so do our purses.
b : And make less money? Never. | Take a bucket too. The roof leaks. | Ha. Put that on a banner.
a : Never. | Two buckets. | Maybe I will.
b?[official] : The Council has the matter in hand.

scene em_rm_pr_herbs_mountain
when topic=prices topic.dir=up topic.item=herbs here.region=ridgemere
a : Herbs come down from the Rainward Hills, and the rain rots half of them. | Wet herbs at #topic.price#. Mould, mostly. | Everything green in Ridgemere is moss.
b : The rain rots everything. | Mould's a herb, if you're poor. | And moss is free.
a : Including tempers. | Don't joke about that. | Then I'm rich.
b?[healer] : Dry them by the fire the day you buy them. Or you'll lose them.

scene em_rm_pr_cheap_ship
when topic=prices topic.dir=down here.region=ridgemere
a : A ship came up the Sound full of grain. Prices dropped by dusk. | #topic.what# for #topic.price#. The wharf's busy for once. | Greatly's new hull brought a hold full of food.
b : Long may the ships come. | For once. | Good old Greatly.
a : Long may they. | Enjoy it. | For once.
b?[sailor] : Rough crossing for that cargo. Eat it slow and think of us.

scene em_rm_pr_houses_rich
when topic=prices here.region=ridgemere
a : Up in the Heights nobody's counting pennies. | Lady Maren's cook bought every egg in the Commons Market. | The Houses' servants buy first and leave us the rest.
b : Never have, never will. | Every egg? | The way it's always been.
a : Must be nice. | Every last one. | Way it'll always be.
b?[servant] : We're told what to buy. We don't eat it.

scene em_sf_pr_tiers
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=ridgemere
a : At the Sump Market #topic.what# is #topic.price#. In the Heights it's twice that and nobody blinks. | Everything costs more the higher you climb in this city. | Up in the Heights Market they sell cakes with gold leaf.
b : In the Heights they pay for the view. | Even the rain. | Gold leaf? Tastes of nothing.
a : The view of us. | Especially the rain. | Like their manners.

scene em_sf_pr_syndicate
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=ridgemere
a : Somebody's skimming every crate off the wharf. That's the price. | They say someone at the Customs House takes a cut of every barrel. | Respectable merchants, respectable prices, and someone in a back room getting fat.
b : Everyone knows. Nobody says. | They say. Quietly. | Someone always is.
a : I'm saying it. | Quietly. | Always.
b?[guard] : Careful who hears you say that.

scene em_ua_pr_crafts_ward
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=ridgemere here.place=market|street
a : In the Sump they're trading tools for food now. | My neighbour paid for #topic.what# with a mended lamp. | Coin's tight in the Sump. Folk barter.
b : Clever. | Did it work? | Coin was always tight down there.
a : Necessary. | The lamp leaks, but yes. | Tighter now.
b?[crafter] : My hinges buy more than my pennies, these days.

scene em_sr_pr_salt
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=ridgemere
a : Salt's the one thing we're never short of. Pity we can't eat it alone. | We rake the salt pans and buy back salt fish at twice the price. | #topic.what# at #topic.price#, and the pans full of white gold.
b : Pity indeed. | That's the trade. | White gold for someone else.
a : Salt soup again. | A bad one. | Always.
b?[laborer] : Rake the pans all day, and buy my supper with what's left.

scene em_sr_pr_boats
when topic=prices topic.dir=up topic.item=meal here.region=ridgemere
a : The boats came in empty. Supper's dear. | No fish, no supper. That's the Sump. | Storm kept the boats in. Prices up by noon.
b : Tomorrow, maybe. | That's the whole Sump in a line. | It always does.
a : If the wind drops. | Put it over the Soup Kitchen door. | Always.
b?[fisher] : Can't catch what won't come. The fish went out of the Sound.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Frosthollow

scene em_ua_pr_haul
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=frosthollow
a : Up the High Road, up the price. #topic.price# for #topic.what#. | The carters blame the switchbacks for every penny. | A carter told me #topic.what# costs half down in the city.
b : Every step of that road is a penny. | And the switchbacks blame the snow. | Then let the carter eat down there.
a : And there are a lot of steps. | And the snow blames nobody. | Gladly.
b?[carter] : You haul a cart up that valley and tell me it's not worth it.

scene em_ua_pr_snow_cheap
when topic=prices topic.dir=down here.region=frosthollow
a : #topic.what# for #topic.price#, up here! Who died? | Cheap #topic.what# at the general store. A miracle. | The carts from the city must have come up full.
b : Nobody. The road opened, that's all. | Get it before it's gone. | First time this season.
a : Then the road is my new friend. | Running. | And the last, probably.

scene em_cb_pr_ore
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=frosthollow
a : Ore's cheap, food's dear. Backwards town. | The city buys our ore for nothing and sells us bread for everything. | Miners can't eat ore.
b : Backwards and frozen. | That's the city's way. | They'd try, if it came to it.
a : And coughing. | Always has been. | We'll see.
b?[miner] : I dug a cart of ore today. Bought half a loaf.

scene em_cb_pr_herbs_cough
when topic=prices topic.dir=up topic.item=herbs here.region=frosthollow
a : Coltsfoot for the cough at #topic.price#. In a town where everyone coughs. | The healer's out of chest herbs again. | Everyone in Frosthollow needs herbs and nobody can afford them.
b : Of course it's dear. Everyone wants it. | Again. | That's Frosthollow.
a : Exactly. | Every season. | That's us.
b?[healer] : Breathe through a damp cloth in the shafts. It's cheaper than any herb.

scene em_cb_pr_cheap
when topic=prices topic.dir=down here.region=frosthollow
a : The grain carts made it up the High Road. Food's cheaper. | #topic.what# for #topic.price#. The mine crews will eat tonight. | Cheaper bread. The smith's whistling.
b : About time the road gave back. | Good. They earned it. | He never whistles.
a : About time. | They did. | He is today.
b?[smith] : A smith with a full belly works twice as hard.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Larkfield and the downs

scene em_ac_pr_toll
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=larkfield
a : Toll's up, so food's up. Every cart passes it on. | The gate toll adds a penny to every crate, and every crate adds a penny to supper. | #topic.what# at #topic.price#. Thank the toll.
b : Pennies on pennies. | And supper adds one to the tavern bill. | Thank the toll for nothing.
a : Pennies on pennies. | Round and round. | For nothing.
b?[official] : The toll pays for the wall. You'd miss the wall.

scene em_ac_pr_carters_eat
when topic=prices topic.dir=up topic.item=meal here.region=larkfield
a : Forty carters at the Singing Lark last night. Not a crumb left. | When the market's full, the stew runs out. | The carters eat everything before the town wakes.
b : Forty! | Then the price goes up. | Then go to bed earlier and wake earlier.
a : Forty hungry carters. | It does. | I can't wake earlier than a carter.
b?[innkeeper] : I cook for sixty and serve eighty. Then they complain.

scene em_ac_pr_cheap
when topic=prices topic.dir=down here.region=larkfield
a : Everything passes through Larkfield market. When there's plenty, we feel it first. | #topic.what# for #topic.price#. The market must be overflowing. | The carts dumped their extra before the long road.
b : First to feel it, first to lose it. | Overflowing with mules, anyway. | Lighter for the road.
a : Always. | And mule dung. | And cheaper for us.

scene em_wm_pr_mercantile
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=larkfield
a : The general store's chalked new prices again. | Old Fennick at the general store wrote my name in the book again. | Half the downs owes the general store, and the prices keep climbing.
b : Up or down? | How long is your line? | That's how they keep us.
a : Up, mostly. | Longer than the book. | That's how.
b?[merchant] : Credit costs. Somebody has to carry it.

scene em_wm_pr_drovers
when topic=prices topic.dir=up topic.item=meal here.region=downs
a : The drovers are late and meat's dear all week. | No drovers this month, so no mutton. | Mutton at #topic.price#. The drovers must be scarce.
b : Turnips, then. | Barley, then. | Scarce as rain.
a : Turnips again. | Barley again. | Scarcer.
b?[herder] : Sheep don't walk themselves to market. Pay the drover.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Coldwater

scene em_lk_pr_fish
when topic=prices topic.dir=up topic.item=meal here.region=coldwater
a : Fish from Glasswater, and still it's #topic.price#. | If the lake's full of fish, why's supper dear? | The boatwrights eat better than the fishers.
b : Ask the fishers. | The lake's moody. | Boats sell for more than fish.
a : They're out on the water. | Like everything here. | That's the trouble.
b?[fisher] : The lake's full. The nets are torn. New nets cost.

scene em_lk_pr_cheap
when topic=prices topic.dir=down here.region=coldwater
a : Big catch on the lake. Fish for nothing. | #topic.what# for #topic.price#. Even the gulls are fat. | The boats came in so heavy they nearly sank.
b : Eat fish till you swim. | Fat gulls and fat pups. | Nearly is fine.
a : Already do. | That's a good week. | Very fine.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mirebridge

scene em_fh_pr_herbs_ours
when topic=prices topic.dir=up topic.item=herbs here.region=mirebridge
a : We grow the herbs. How are they #topic.price# in our own town? | Mirebridge herbs go out by the cartload and come back dearer. | The herbalists sell the best to the city and keep the stems.
b : Because the city pays more. | Every cart, every season. | Stems for the locals.
a : Always the city. | Every season. | Stems and promises.
b?[healer] : The city pays. We don't. That's the whole of it.

scene em_fh_pr_herbs_cheap
when topic=prices topic.item=herbs topic.dir=down here.region=mirebridge
a : Herbs cheap enough to stuff a mattress. | The fen gave a good season. Every shed's full. | #topic.price# a bundle. The herbalists are grumbling.
b : I'll stuff mine. | Bless the fen. | They always grumble.
a : Sleep well, then. | For once. | And always eat.

scene em_fh_pr_peat
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=mirebridge
a : Peat's wet and supper's dear. A good week for misery. | Can't dry peat, can't cook. Can't cook, buy food. Can't buy food. | The fen road's flooded and no carts are coming.
b : A good week for marsh lights, too. | That's Mirebridge all over. | Then we wait.
a : Don't follow them. | All over. | And we're hungry.
b?[laborer] : Cut peat all morning. Wet as a fish.

scene em_sf_pr_river
when topic=prices topic.dir=down here.region=mirebridge
a : The barges came down the Long River full. Prices fell. | #topic.what# for #topic.price# by the river. | River's been kind this month. Food's cheap.
b : Bless the river. | River's always cheapest. | Kind for once.
a : And the bargemen. | And muddiest. | For once.
b?[sailor] : The river's always kind until it isn't.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Southmeadow

scene em_af_pr_grain
when topic=prices topic.dir=up topic.item=meal here.region=southmeadow
a : We grow the grain and pay #topic.price# for a meal. | The grain goes north and the bread comes back dearer. | The price chalked at the bakery door's gone up again.
b : That's trade. | The carters take a cut both ways. | I saw.
a : That's robbery. | Both ways. | Everyone saw.
b?[farmer] : They buy my wheat cheap in the field and sell it dear in the loaf.

scene em_af_pr_dry
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=southmeadow
a : No rain, no harvest, no cheap bread. | The wells are low and the fields are cracked. | The farmers are praying and the prices are climbing.
b : Rain will come. | Bad year. | Pray with them.
a : When? | Very bad. | I am.
b?[farmer] : One more dry week and I'll lose the whole field.

scene em_af_pr_harvest
when topic=prices topic.dir=down here.region=southmeadow here.season=summer|autumn
a : Harvest's in. Bread's cheap. Southmeadow smiles. | The granary's full to the rafters. | #topic.what# for #topic.price#. The fields did us proud.
b : Smile while you can. | Full granary, fat winter. | Proud and tired.
a : While I can. | Let's hope. | Very tired.
b?[farmer] : Every ear of it cut by paw and tooth. Remember that when you eat it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Oakhaven

scene em_hm_pr_carter
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=oakhaven
a : The carter's late, so whatever he brings will cost more. | Prices in Oakhaven are whatever the carter says. | The carter brought salt and said a number. We paid it.
b : He's always late. | And he says big numbers. | What else could we do?
a : And always dear. | Bigger every time. | Nothing.

scene em_hm_pr_garden
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.region=oakhaven
a : I'll grow more in the garden. Can't trust the carter's prices. | Every house in Oakhaven should keep a garden. | Herbs and beans from the garden. No pennies needed.
b : Good idea. | Most do. | Beans again?
a : About time. | The rest should. | Beans forever.
b?[old] : The Warmwood fed this town before there was a road. It can again.
